! ja_bb6b_worst_pattern.strap -- IBM 7030 "WORST PATTERN TEST",
! File No. JA BB6B, August 15, 1961 (docs/ja_bb6b_worst_pat_test.pdf,
! 20 PDF pages: writeup pp.1-2, the PRNID cards p.3, listing pp.4-20).
! PRNID: "WORST PATTERN (6 BOX) A. BROWN".  The writeup's cover says it
! makes "JA CB6 Worst Pattern Test" obsolete.
!
! TRANSCRIBED VERBATIM from the page images rendered at 100, 200 and
! 400 dpi (no OCR), with this repo's print-chain conventions: "%"
! prints "(", the box glyph prints ")".  THIS CHAIN PRINTS THE REMARK
! MARK AS "-" (the 8-4 punch; mcp_bootstrap_p236.strap has the source),
! the same glyph as a minus, and the machine-code column decides each
! one: "M06AZ-START1" and "$-0.32" are minus signs (their code needs
! them), every other "-" opens a remark.  Remarks follow "! @" here.
!
! GLYPHS AND DEPARTURES, each settled against the machine-code column:
!   - THE SECOND "PH1E" AND "PH2E".  PDF p.9 prints the label of
!     SX,$X8,0($X2) at 001134.00 as "PH1E" (read at 400 dpi: a clear
!     bottom stroke), a second definition of PH1E, which is also the
!     label at 001123.00.  The SWAPI rows that name the pair print
!     "PH1E,PH1F" (PDF p.10, 400 dpi) and their code "001134.02 E0"
!     puts PH1F at 001134.00.  So the card said PH1F; the deck writes
!     PH1F, the printed label kept as a remark.  PDF p.17's label at
!     100115.00 ("PH2E", against SWAPI,1,PH2E,PH2F's 100115.02) is the
!     same case.
!   - "T (SIX" word (PDF p.12): the source digits read at 400 dpi are
!     53000025513D5B00; the code 0514000002252117255400 agrees.
!   No printed code disagrees with its source line, and no row is torn
!   or unreadable.
!
! LISTING-ORACLE RESULT (tests/verify_ja_bb6b_listing.py): every printed
! row on PDF pp.4-20 is reproduced bit-for-bit by strap_asm.py: 574
! checks, all PASS -- 485 printed rows, 87 symbol addresses (the SYNs
! TYPE, M06AZ and M06AZ2 among them), ACC1's one-word DR, and END,100.'s
! 144.00.  Unchecked: rows that print no code (PRNID, SEM, PUNFUL, SLC,
! CNOP on a full word, the blank listing lines in the NOP runs).
!
! WHAT THE PROGRAM DOES (writeup PDF pp.1-2, read with the code).
!   "The purpose of this test is to check for data pickup or dropout
!   when a checkerboard or inverted checkerboard is present in memory.
!   It is designed to run on a system having two 16K-A memories and
!   four 16K-B memories." (p.1, 1.)  "The program alternately tests
!   upper and lower memories" (p.1, 2.1).  "A checkerboard pattern is
!   stored and checked, and inverted and checked." (p.2, 4.)
!   Part I, START1 in low core, saves 500 words of Part II (100000) at
!   START1+500. and tests 100000-277013 (CTLB1, CTLC1; upper limit
!   CTLH1 = 97803, so the top 500 words, 277014-277777, are not
!   tested); restores Part II and branches to it.  Part II, START2 at
!   100000, saves 900 words from 100 (octal) at START2+500. and tests
!   100-77777 (CTLB2, CTLC2); restores, adds one to the pass counter
!   and branches back to PH1.  Forever.  Each half runs:
!   1. "DOUBLE ERROR CHECKING": CM1111 / CM0000 with progressive
!      indexing (V+ICR) write runs of 8 all-ones then 8 all-zeros words
!      (Part I; runs of 4 in Part II, CTLA2), from the first address
!      to a SPLIT -- 177777 in Part I, 37777 in Part II -- where X2's
!      count runs out and BR1 SWAPIs the two stores, re-phasing the
!      runs for the second region (200000-277013; 40000-77777).  The
!      check reads each word with CT1100 / CT0011 and, if it is wrong,
!      hangs on BRGZ,$; else it inverts the word in place four times
!      with CM1100 ("WORK LOCATION ADJACENT TO LOCATION CHECKED").
!      Then the whole is redone complemented (the SWAPIs at BR4), and
!      every tested word is zeroed (CBR+ loop).
!   2. "SINGLE ERROR INJECTION": the same runs are stored with SX,$X8
!      (all ones) / Z, each store bracketed by SX,$X7,$UB ("TURN ON
!      ERROR INJECTION") and Z,$UB, followed by ten NOPs; then BR11
!      inverts each word 8 (4) times ("FOR PICK UP") and BR12 rewrites
!      it unchanged ("RECHECK ALL LOCATIONS"), with interrupts ENABLED
!      (BE,BR11) and the interrupt table INT1/INT2 all NOPs.  There is
!      no program check in this part: it relies on the machine's ECC.
!      Then complemented, then every tested word zeroed.
!   PASS AND FAIL, IN THE PROGRAM'S OWN WORDS: "If an error is
!   encountered, the program will stop.  Refer to the listing and neons
!   to determine the nature of the failure.  No error print-out is
!   provided." (p.1, 2.2).  The stop is the hang at one of the four
!   "BRGZ,$ -IF HANG UP,ADDR. AT M6AZZ IS NOT 1- S" rows.  "Index Reg 14
!   is used as a pass counter.  Stepping of Index 14 indicates success."
!   (p.2, 3.3.)
!
! THE ERROR INJECTION IS REAL HARDWARE, NOT A BOUNDARY SETTING.  CE
! Introduction to Programming Vol. 3, R23-9695 (docs/), section 9 "ERROR
! INJECTION", printed pp.114-115 (PDF pp.114-115): in maintenance mode,
! with the console's error injection switch on, "Bit 58 of location 3
! (the error injection trigger)" makes bits 0-8 of location 3 (the
! upper boundary register's bits) invert check bits at the output of
! the I checker: bit 0 "Suppress ECC and I parity error indications",
! bit 8 "Invert: P10 (60-63) and CT".  CTLE1 / CTLE2, XW,(8)401000.,0,
! 000040, puts 401000 in bits 0-17 (bits 0 and 8) and decimal 40 in the
! refill field (bits 58 and 60).  So each stored word gets one bad ECC
! check bit: a single error, which the memory corrects on the read.
! The same section explains the NOPs: "the instruction which is to
! terminate error injection [must] be positioned in the program in
! such a manner that it does not receive a parity error", since
! instructions in the I unit and look-ahead when the trigger is set
! are immune.  And the writeup's loading step 1.2.7 is "Disable two
! levels of lookahead." (p.1).
!
! WHAT THE MODEL LACKS, AND WHAT THAT MEANS FOR THE RUN:
!   - NO ECC AND NO ERROR INJECTION.  StretchStorage keeps only bits
!     0-17, 32-49 and 57 of location 3 (boundary_width.strap), so bit
!     58 is dropped and the stores are ordinary.  The single-error part
!     runs and its stores are checked as data, but what it exists to
!     test (correction of an injected single error, the error stop) is
!     NOT exercised.  Bits 0-17 do land in the model's upper boundary:
!     401000 with the lower boundary 0 and control bit 0 -- every
!     address inside -- but the stores run with interrupts disabled
!     (BD,CK1C; BD,CK2C), and the model protects only when enabled
!     (Reference Manual printed p.45), so no store is suppressed.
!   - NO MAINTENANCE MODE, NO CONSOLE SWITCHES (error injection, error
!     stop) and no look-ahead disable.  The sense switches (word 4) are
!     the model's 0: "Switch 36 Active bypasses Error Injecting tests.
!     Switch 37 Active Loops on test of Upper Memory.  Switch 38 Active
!     Loops on test of Lower Memory." (writeup p.2, 3.2) -- BB 4.36
!     goes to BR13P (Part I) / BR13Q (Part II), past the injection;
!     4.37 loops PH1, 4.38 loops START2 -- none is taken.  BB,4.32,PH1
!     ("BYPASS PRINT IF ACTIVE") is not in the writeup; 0, not taken.
!   - A TYPEWRITER ON CHANNEL 39.  TYPE is "SYN,19.32" (PDF p.12), as
!     in ja_bm6a; the one W,TYPE,CWA1 (the title) is a reject on the
!     model.  Nothing else is typed.
!   - BEW's WAIT.  "BEW,$+0.32-START OF TEST" (PDF p.5) waits for an
!     interruption on the machine; the model's BEW does not wait
!     (StretchExecute.bsv), so the run goes straight on.
!
! MEMORY FACTS (for A11a).  No statement about unit busy, cycle or
! recycle time.  What the document does state or show:
!   - "two 16K-A memories and four 16K-B memories" (p.1); the lower
!     test covers 100-77777 and the upper 100000-277777, as in ja_bp6a
!     and ja_bm6a -- the reverse of StretchMemory.bsv's map (four-way
!     over 0-177777).
!   - THE RUN LENGTHS: 8 words in the upper memories (CTLA1, "6M"), 4
!     in the lower (CTLA2), and the SPLITS at 200000 and 40000, where
!     the pattern is re-phased.  INFERENCE, not stated anywhere: 8 = two
!     words in each of four interleaved B boxes and 4 = two in each of
!     two interleaved A boxes would make the runs a physical
!     checkerboard; the splits would then be box-pair boundaries.  The
!     document gives no interleaving.
!
! HOW IT IS RUN: see tests/run_ja_bb6b.sh and check_ja_bb6b_dump.py.
!   WHAT IS STUBBED: the IPL (PUNFUL commented out, image preloaded, as
!   ja_bp6a), and the ENTRY, an inference: END,100. names word 100
!   (144), where this deck loads nothing, so the run starts at START1,
!   which the load chain's CW at 777 loads from.
!   RESULT (2026-11-26): stopped after Part I's checkerboards (CHECK,
!   31,776,224 clocks), after Part I's injection part (INJECT,
!   103,925,782) and after one whole pass (PASS, 149,241,141), the
!   program has not hung, X14 has stepped once (1 << 29: the decimal
!   one lands in bits 31-34 of the field at bits 17-34), and every word
!   of core it has reached is as computed from the listing.  An injected
!   stuck bit (IBM bit 20 stuck at 0 on stores to 150000-150777) makes
!   the program hang on CK1A's BRGZ,$ with M6AZZ naming 150000;
!   check_ja_bb6b_dump.py has the record.  THE MODEL'S halted() DOES NOT
!   RISE ON THAT HANG: the run goes on to its step cap with the PC on
!   the BRGZ, so the checker reads the PC rather than waiting for a
!   halt.

        PRNID,WORST PATTERN (6 BOX) A. BROWN
        PRNID,AUG 15, 1961, JA BB6B
        SEM,6,G
!       PUNFUL,                    ! PRINTED (PDF p.4): COMMENTED OUT, see HOW IT IS RUN
        SLC,511.
        CW(CDSC),512.,M06AZ-START1,CW2Q
START1  BD,$+0.32
        Z,$MASK                    ! @RESET MASK
        Z,$IND                     ! @RESET INDICATORS
        Z,$UB                      ! @RESET BOUNDS
        LVI,$X10,INT1
        SV,$X10,$IA                ! @SET UP INTERRUPT ADDRESS
        BMKZ,$+0.32
        BIKZ,$+0.32
        BIJZ,$+0.32
        BEKZ,$+0.32
        BTSZ,$+0.32
        BCPUZ,$+0.32
        BEKJZ,$+0.32
        BUNRJZ,$+0.32
        BCBJZ,$+0.32
        BEPGKZ,$+0.32
        BUKZ,$+0.32
        BEEZ,$+0.32
        BEOPZ,$+0.32
        BCSZ,$+0.32
        BOPZ,$+0.32
        BADZ,$+0.32
        BUSAZ,$+0.32
        BEXEZ,$+0.32
        BDSZ,$+0.32
        NOP
            NOP,                   ! @B,PH1 FOR NON PRINT
        LCI,$X14,0                 ! @USED AS PASS COUNTER
        BB,4.32,PH1                ! @BYPASS PRINT IF ACTIVE
        W,TYPE,CWA1                ! @CONTROLS PATTERN
        BEW,$+0.32                 ! @START OF TEST
        BD,PH1
! @DOUBLE ERROR CHECKING FOR UPPER MEMORY
PH1     LCI,$X15,500
        T,$X15,START2,START1+500.  ! @SAVE LOWER TEST
        LX,$X1,CTLA1               ! @CKERBOARD PATTERN
        LX,$X2,CTLB1               ! @SPLIT OR UPPER MEMORY
        LX,$X4,CTLD1               ! @UPPER LIMIT
        LX,$X6,CTLD1               ! @COMPLEMENTING
        BE,PH1A
PH1AR   LX,$X1,CTLA1
                NOP,0.0            ! @TO REPEAT THIS PHASE
! @CHECKERBOARD GENERATING ROUTINE
        CNOP
PH1A    CM1111(V+ICR)(BU,64,8),1.($X2)   ! @STORE ALL ONES WORD
        BXCZ,BR1                   ! @CT 0 SPLIT OR UPPER MEM.
        CBR,$X1,PH1A
                CNOP               ! @CONTROLS PATTERN
PH1B    CM0000(V+ICR)(BU,64,8),1.($X2)   ! @STORE ALL ZEROES WORD
        BXCZ,BR1                   ! @CT 0 SPLIT OR UPPER MEM.
        CBR,$X1,PH1B               ! @CONTROLS PATTERN
        B,PH1A                     ! @NO LIMIT REACHED-REPEAT
BR1     CBRZ,$X4,BR2               ! @IFCT 1 SPLIT-IF 0 UPPER MEM.
        SWAPI,1,PH1B,PH1A          ! @SET UP FOR SPLIT
        B,PH1A                     ! @RETURN TO GENERATE LOOP
BR2     SWAPI,1,PH1A,PH1B          ! @RESTORE LOOP
! @CHECKING ROUTINE
CK1     LX,$X1,CTLA1               ! @CONTROLS CHECK PATTERN
        LX,$X2,CTLB1
                CNOP               ! @CONTROLS STEPPING
CK1A    CT1100(V+ICR)(BU,64,8),1.($X2)   ! @CK ONES WORD
        BXCZ,BR3
                NOP                ! @CK FOR SPLIT OR UPPER LIMIT
        SX,$X2,M6AZZ
                    BRGZ,$         ! @IF HANG UP,ADDR. AT M6AZZ  IS NOT 1- S
        V-I,$X2,1.
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)     ! @WORK LOCATION ADJACENT
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)     ! @TO LOCATION CHECKED
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)
        V+I,$X2,1.                 ! @RESTORE VALUE OF X2
        CBR,$X1,CK1A
                CNOP
CK1B    CT0011(V+ICR)(BU,64,8),1.($X2)   ! @CK ZEROES WORD
        BXCZ,BR3
                NOP                ! @CK FOR SPLIT OR UPPER LIMIT
        SX,$X2,M6AZZ
                    BRGZ,$         ! @IF HANG UP,ADDR. AT M6AZZ  IS NOT 0- S
        V-I,$X2,1.
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)     ! @WORK LOCATION ADJACENT TO
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)     ! @LOCATION CHECKED
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)
        V+I,$X2,1.                 ! @RESTORE VALUE OF X2
        CBR,$X1,CK1B
        B,CK1A                     ! @REPEAT LOOP
BR3     CBRZ,$X4,BR4               ! @CT IS ONE SPLIT 0 UPPER LIMIT
        SWAPI,3,CK1A,CK1B          ! @SET UP LOOP FOR SPLIT
        B,CK1A                     ! @RETURN TO LOOP
BR4     SWAPI,3,CK1A,CK1B          ! @RESTORE LOOP
        CBRZ,$X6,BR5               ! @IF CT IS 1 SET UP PH1 AND CK1
        SWAPI,1,PH1A,PH1B          ! @FOR COMPL. TEST
        SWAPI,3,CK1A,CK1B
        B,PH1AR                    ! @REPEAT PHASE
BR5     SWAPI,1,PH1A,PH1B          ! @RESTORE ORIGINAL LOOP
        SWAPI,3,CK1A,CK1B          ! @RESTORE ORIGINAL CONNECTIVES
        LX,$X2,CTLI1               ! @RESET ALL LOCATIONS
        Z,0($X2)
        CBR+,$X2,$-0.32
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        BB,4.36,BR13P              ! @LOOP ON CHECKERBOARDS
        BD,CK1C                    ! @TO SINGLE ERROR TEST
! @SET UP FOR SINGLE ERROR INJECTION
CK1C    LX,$X7,CTLE1               ! @FOR ERROR INJECTION
        CM1111(BU,64,8),$X8        ! @FOR ONES WORD
        LX,$X2,CTLB1               ! @FIRST ADDRESS
        LX,$X1,CTLA1               ! @PATTERN
BR6     SX,$X7,$UB                 ! @TURN ON ERROR INJECTION
        CNOP
PH1C    SX,$X8,0($X2)
        CNOP
        Z,$UB
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        KV,$X2,CTLG1               ! @CHECK FOR SPLIT
        BXEZ,BR8                   ! @TO NEW PATTERN
        V+I,$X2,1.                 ! @INCREMENT ADDRESS FOR NEXT STORE
        CBR,$X1,BR6                ! @LOOP
BR7     SX,$X7,$UB                 ! @TURN ON ERROR INJECTION
        CNOP
PH1D    Z,0($X2)
        CNOP
        Z,$UB
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        KV,$X2,CTLG1               ! @CHECK FOR SPLIT
        BXEZ,BR8                   ! @TO NEW PATTERN
        V+I,$X2,1.                 ! @INC. ADDRESS FOR NEXT STORE
        CBR,$X1,BR7                ! @LOOP
        B,BR6                      ! @REPEAT UNTIL SPLIT IS REACHED
BR8     LX,$X2,CTLC1               ! @SET UP FOR REMAINDER OF MEM
BR9     SX,$X7,$UB                 ! @TURN ON ERROR INJECTION
        CNOP
PH1E    Z,0($X2)
        CNOP
        Z,$UB
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        KV,$X2,CTLH1               ! @CK FOR UPPER LIMIT
        BXEZ,CK1D                  ! @TO CHECK PATTERN
        V+I,$X2,1.                 ! @INCR ADDRESS
        CBR,$X1,BR9                ! @LOOP
BR10    SX,$X7,$UB                 ! @TURN ON ERROR INJECTION
        CNOP
PH1F    SX,$X8,0($X2)              ! LABEL PRINTED "PH1E" (PDF p.9); see header
        CNOP
        Z,$UB
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        KV,$X2,CTLH1               ! @CK FOR UPPER LIMIT
        BXEZ,CK1D                  ! @TO CHECK PATTERN
        V+I,$X2,1.                 ! @INCR ADDRESS
        CBR,$X1,BR10
        B,BR9                      ! @REPEAT UNTIL UPPER LIMIT REACHED
! @SINGLE ERROR CHECKING
CK1D    LX,$X2,CTLI1               ! @CTL ADDRESS STEPPING
        BE,BR11
BR11    CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)     ! @INVERT DATA AND CHECK
        CBR,$X1,BR11               ! @FOR PICK UP
        CBR+,$X2,BR11              ! @REPEAT UNTIL UPPER LIMIT
BR12    CM0011(BU,64,8),0($X2)     ! @RECHECK ALL LOCATIONS
        CBR+,$X2,BR12
! @COMPLEMENT TEST
COMP1   CBRZ,$X6,BR13              ! @COMPL. TEST CTRL
        SWAPI,1,PH1C,PH1D          ! @SET UP FOR COMPL (SINGLE)
        SWAPI,1,PH1E,PH1F
        BD,CK1C                    ! @START COMPL TEST
BR13    SWAPI,1,PH1C,PH1D          ! @RESTORE
        SWAPI,1,PH1E,PH1F
BR13P   LX,$X2,CTLI1               ! @RESET ALL LOCATIONS
        Z,0($X2)
        CBR+,$X2,$-0.32
BR14    LCI,$X15,500
        T,$X15,START1+500.,START2  ! @RELOCATE LOWER TEST
        BB,4.37,PH1                ! @LOOP ON UPPER MEMORY
        BD,START2
! @INTERRUPT TABLE UPPER TEST
INT1    NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        CNOP
TITLA1  DD(BU,64,8),0,0,0
        (16)DD(BU,64,8),0000000000000000   ! @
        (16)DD(BU,64,8),453545494F5D0059   ! @MEMORY W
        (16)DD(BU,64,8),494F5153004B2D53   ! @ORST PAT
        (16)DD(BU,64,8),53354F4700533551   ! @TERN TES
        (16)DD(BU,64,8),53000025513D5B00   ! @T (SIX
        (16)DD(BU,64,8),2F495B35512700FD   ! @BOXES) RET
        DD(BU),0,0,0
! @INDEX AND CONTROL WORDS FOR UPPER TEST 6 MEMORIES
CWA1    CW(CR),TITLA1,9,CWA1       ! @TITLE
CTLA1   XW,0.,8,CTLA1              ! @6M
CTLB1   XW,32768.,32768.,CTLC1     ! @SPLIT CONTROL-6M
CTLC1   XW,65536.,32268.,CTLB1     ! @REMAINING ADDRESSES
CTLD1   XW,0.,2,CTLD1
CTLE1   XW,(8)401000.,0,000040     ! @CT
CTLG1   VF,65535.                  ! @6M
CTLH1   VF,97803.                  ! @6M
CTLI1   XW,32768.,65036.,CTLI1     ! @6M
NOCOM   (16)DD(BU,64,8),60 62 64 66 68 6A 6C 6E   ! @01234567
ACC1    DR(BU,64,8),(1)
CW2Q    CW(CD),32768.,M06AZ2-START2,$
        NOP
        NOP
M06AZ   SYN,M6AZZ+1.0
M6AZZ   NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
TYPE    SYN,19.32
        SLC,32768.
! @DOUBLE ERROR CHECKING FOR LOWER MEMORY
START2  LCI,$X15,900
        T,$X15,64.0,START2+500.    ! @SAVE UPPER TEST
        LX,$X1,CTLA2               ! @CHECKERBOARD PATTERN
        LX,$X2,CTLB2               ! @SPLIT OR UPPER MEM
        LX,$X4,CTLD2               ! @UPPER LIMIT
        LX,$X6,CTLD2               ! @COMPLEMENTING
        Z,$UB                      ! @RESET BOUNDS
        LVI,$X10,INT2
        SV,$X10,$IA                ! @SET INTRT ADDRESS
        BE,PH2A
! @CHECKERBOARD GENERATING ROUTINE
PH2AR   LX,$X1,CTLA2
                NOP,0.0            ! @TO REPEAT THIS PHASE
        CNOP
PH2A    CM1111(V+ICR)(BU,64,8),1.($X2)   ! @ST ALL ONES
        BXCZ,BR1A                  ! @CT0 SPLIT OR UPPER MEM
        CBR,$X1,PH2A
                CNOP               ! @CTRL PATTERN
PH2B    CM0000(V+ICR)(BU,64,8),1.($X2)   ! @ST ALL ZEROES
        BXCZ,BR1A
        CBR,$X1,PH2B
        B,PH2A                     ! @NO LIMIT REACHED-REPEAT
BR1A    CBRZ,$X4,BR2A              ! @IF 1 SPLIT-0 UPPER MEM
        SWAPI,1,PH2B,PH2A          ! @SET UP FOR SPLIT
        B,PH2A                     ! @RETURN TO GEN LOOP
BR2A    SWAPI,1,PH2A,PH2B          ! @RESTORE LOOP
! @CHECKING ROUTINE
CK2     LX,$X1,CTLA2               ! @CTRL CHECK PATTERN
        LX,$X2,CTLB2
                CNOP               ! @CTRL STEPPING
CK2A    CT1100(V+ICR)(BU,64,8),1.($X2)   ! @CK ONE WORD
        BXCZ,BR3A
                NOP                ! @CK SPLIT OR UPPER LIMIT
        SX,$X2,M6AZZ2
                    BRGZ,$         ! @IF HANG UP,ADDR. AT 100222 IS NOT 1- S
        V-I,$X2,1.
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)     ! @WORK LOCATION ADJACENT
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)     ! @TO ONE CHECKED
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)
        V+I,$X2,1.                 ! @RESTORE VALUE OF X2
        CBR,$X1,CK2A
                CNOP
CK2B    CT0011(V+ICR)(BU,64,8),1.($X2)   ! @CK ZERO WORD
        BXCZ,BR3A
                NOP                ! @CK FOR SPLIT OR UPPER MEM
        SX,$X2,M6AZZ2
                    BRGZ,$         ! @IF HANG UP,ADDR. AT 100222 IS NOT 0- S
        V-I,$X2,1.
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)     ! @WORK LOCATION TO
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)     ! @ONE CHECKED
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)
        CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)
        V+I,$X2,1.                 ! @RESTORE VALUE OF X2
        CBR,$X1,CK2B
        B,CK2A                     ! @REPEAT LOOP
BR3A    CBRZ,$X4,BR4A              ! @CT 1 SPLIT 0 UPPER MEM
        SWAPI,3,CK2A,CK2B          ! @SETUP FOR SPLIT
        B,CK2A                     ! @RETURN TO LOOP
BR4A    SWAPI,3,CK2A,CK2B          ! @RESTORE LOOP
        CBRZ,$X6,BR5A              ! @IF CT 1 SETUP FOR COMPL
        SWAPI,1,PH2A,PH2B
        SWAPI,3,CK2A,CK2B
        B,PH2AR                    ! @REPEAT PHASE
BR5A    SWAPI,1,PH2A,PH2B          ! @RESTORE LOOP
        SWAPI,3,CK2A,CK2B
        LX,$X2,CTLI2               ! @RESET ALL LOCATIONS
        Z,0($X2)
        CBR+,$X2,$-0.32
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        BB,4.36,BR13Q              ! @LOOP ON CHECKERBOARDS
        BD,CK2C                    ! @TO SINGLE ERROR TEST
! @SET UP FOR SINGLE ERROR INJECTION
CK2C    LX,$X7,CTLE2               ! @FOR ERROR INJ. INV. CO
        CM1111(BU,64,8),$X8        ! @FOR ONES WORD
        LX,$X2,CTLB2               ! @FIRST ADDRESS
        LX,$X1,CTLA2               ! @PATTERN
BR6A    SX,$X7,$UB                 ! @TURN ON ERROR INJECTION
        CNOP
PH2C    SX,$X8,0($X2)
        CNOP
        Z,$UB
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        KV,$X2,CTLG2               ! @CK FOR SPLIT
        BXEZ,BR8A                  ! @TO NEW PATTERN
        V+I,$X2,1.                 ! @INCREMENT ADDRESS
        CBR,$X1,BR6A               ! @LOOP
BR7A    SX,$X7,$UB                 ! @TURN ON ERROR INJECTION
        CNOP
PH2D    Z,0($X2)
        CNOP
        Z,$UB
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        KV,$X2,CTLG2               ! @CHK FOR SPLIT
        BXEZ,BR8A                  ! @TO NEW PATTERN
        V+I,$X2,1.                 ! @INCR. ADDRESS
        CBR,$X1,BR7A               ! @LOOP
        B,BR6A                     ! @REPEAT UNTIL SPLIT
BR8A    LX,$X2,CTLC2               ! @SET UP FOR REMAINDER OF MEM
BR9A    SX,$X7,$UB                 ! @TURN ON ERROR INJECTION
        CNOP
PH2E    Z,0($X2)
        CNOP
        Z,$UB
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        KV,$X2,CTLH2               ! @UPPER MEM
        BXEZ,CK2D                  ! @TO CK PATTERN
        V+I,$X2,1.                 ! @INCR ADDRESS
        CBR,$X1,BR9A               ! @LOOP
BR10A   SX,$X7,$UB                 ! @TURN ON ERROR INJECTION
        CNOP
PH2F    SX,$X8,0($X2)              ! LABEL PRINTED "PH2E" (PDF p.17); see header
        CNOP
        Z,$UB
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        NOP
            NOP
                NOP
                    NOP
                        NOP
!                                  [blank listing line]
        KV,$X2,CTLH2               ! @MEM LIMIT
        BXEZ,CK2D                  ! @TO CHECK PATTERN
        V+I,$X2,1.                 ! @INCR ADDRESS
        CBR,$X1,BR10A
        B,BR9A                     ! @REPEAT UNTIL UPPER MEM
! @SINGLE ERROR CHECKING
CK2D    LX,$X2,CTLI2               ! @CTL ADDR STEPPING
        BE,BR11A
BR11A   CM1100(BU,64,8),0($X2)     ! @INVERT DATA AND CK
        CBR,$X1,BR11A              ! @FOR ERROR
        CBR+,$X2,BR11A             ! @REPEAT UNTIL UPPER LIMIT
BR12A   CM0011(BU,64,8),0($X2)     ! @RECHECK ALL LOCATIONS
        CBR+,$X2,BR12A
! @COMPLEMENT TEST
COMP2   CBRZ,$X6,BR13A             ! @CTRL COMPL
        SWAPI,1,PH2C,PH2D          ! @SET UP FOR COMPL
        SWAPI,1,PH2E,PH2F
        BD,CK2C                    ! @START COMPL
BR13A   SWAPI,1,PH2C,PH2D          ! @RESTORE
        SWAPI,1,PH2E,PH2F
BR13Q   LX,$X2,CTLI2               ! @RESET ALL LOCATIONS
        Z,0($X2)
        CBR+,$X2,$-0.32
BR14A   M+1(DU,18,4),$X14+0.17     ! @UPDATE PASS COUNTER
        LCI,$X15,900
        T,$X15,START2+500,64.0     ! @RESTORE UPPER TEST
        BB,4.38,START2             ! @LOOP ON LOWER MEMORY
        BD,PH1                     ! @RESTART TEST
! @INTERRUPT TABLE LOWER TEST
INT2    NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
        NOP,0.0
                NOP,0.0
